Live draw: CLEAR_SURFACE scales the guest scissor to the sample grid of an antialiased surface, as draws do.
Toro's own patch (7xxx).
What: sink_clear_impl intersects the clear with the surface clip and the guest scissor (patch 2006). The clip from
rsx_dsp_get_surface is in samples (x aa_sx/aa_sy, KZ3 patch 2016) but the scissor was used in pixels; the draw path
already multiplies it (rsx_live_draw.c "The scissor is in pixels too: scale it to the sample grid"). The clear now
multiplies the scissor by aa_sx/aa_sy too, for the colour and the depth/stencil clear.
Why (run tlp-book, frame 3379-3381, work/book/, the RE notes "Story memory book"): every frame
clears 0x01FB0000 (SURFACE_FORMAT 0xA0B5148, antialias 5, 2560x1440 samples used of a 5120x2880 host surface) with
mask 0xF3 and scissor 0x05000000/0x02D00000 (1280x720 pixels). Unscaled, colour and depth were cleared only in the
top-left 1280x720 samples. The book page (fp 0x090751C0, 54 verts, texture 1:0x05EEA880 1280x720) and the photo
quad are drawn full screen with depth test LESS (z/w ~0.55): they appear inside the cleared quarter and fail against
the title scene's stale depth everywhere else, where the title's colour also stays. The downsample (2560x1440 window,
patch 7002) then shows the book in the top-left quarter of the frame and the old title scene around it; the same
stale scene sits behind the main menu and the loading screen. The title itself redraws every sample (sky), so it
never showed.
Switch: none (LD_CLEAR_NO_SCISSOR=1 still disables the clear scissor entirely).
Verify: build; run to the Story memory book: the book fills the screen, no title streamers/characters behind the
main menu, loading screen or book. The title screen is unchanged (alias-subrect window 2560x1440 still used).

